<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">ERP & Tech</div><h1>SAP vs Zoho vs ERPNext vs Tally: An Honest, Vendor-Neutral Guide for MSMEs</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>This comparison is vendor-neutral. We have no referral arrangements with any of these providers. Our recommendation is always based solely on client fit.</p><h4>Tally Prime — Best For</h4><p>Businesses whose primary need is accounting and compliance. If your main pain is GST filing, financial reporting, and basic inventory tracking — Tally is the right answer. It is affordable, widely understood by Indian accountants, and does not require implementation consultants. Do not over-engineer a Tally problem into a SAP solution.</p><h4>Zoho One — Best For</h4><p>Growing businesses that need CRM, inventory, HR, and operations in one connected ecosystem. Zoho's Indian pricing is extremely competitive and implementation complexity is manageable. Best suited for businesses in the ₹5Cr–₹50Cr range with 20–200 employees.</p><h4>ERPNext — Best For</h4><p>Manufacturing or distribution businesses that need genuine ERP functionality without SAP pricing. ERPNext is open-source, highly customisable, and has a strong Indian implementation partner ecosystem. Requires a competent implementation partner — do not attempt self-implementation.</p><h4>SAP Business One / S/4HANA — Best For</h4><p>Businesses above ₹100Cr revenue with complex multi-location, multi-entity operations that need a system capable of scaling to ₹1000Cr+. The implementation cost and timeline are significant — budget ₹30L–₹1Cr+ and 6–18 months. Never implement SAP because a competitor uses it.</p><h4>Our Advice</h4><p>The most expensive ERP mistake is choosing a system based on brand recognition rather than business fit. Always start with a 2-week needs assessment before evaluating any vendor. The right system is the one that solves your specific problems — not the most sophisticated one on the market.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
</Layout>
